## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical cross-account data sharing with fine-grained data protection, lineage, and incident readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM roles and least privilege
- Field-level masking, KMS, Lake Formation
- PII discovery with Macie, immutable logs with CloudTrail/S3 Object Lock

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example pseudo: mask sensitive fields in records
function maskFields(record, fields) {
  const out = {...record};
  for (const f of fields) if (f in out) out[f] = '***';
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the masking policy against evolving data models?
- How would you invalidate stale tokens during a breach simulation?

Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design time-bound cross-account access for external partners and maintain auditability across accounts.

Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- STS AssumeRole with session duration
- S3 Access Points and bucket policies per tenant
- KMS CMK rotation and envelope encryption
- CloudTrail multi-account logging and integrity
- Automated expiry and revocation mechanisms; breach simulations

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: using AWS SDK v3 to assume a role and upload to S3
import { STSClient, AssumeRoleCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sts";
import { S3Client, PutObjectCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";

async function uploadWithTemporaryCredentials(roleArn, bucket, key, body) {
  const sts = new STSClient({ region: "us-east-1" });
  const cred = await sts.send(new AssumeRoleCommand({ RoleArn: roleArn, RoleSessionName: "partnerUpload", DurationSeconds: 900 }));
  const s3 = new S3Client({ region: "us-east-1", credentials: cred.Credentials });
  await s3.send(new PutObjectCommand({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key, Body: body }));
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and respond to a compromised tenant session expiry breach?
- What changes would you make to support a new partner with slightly different data retention requirements?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, secure cross-account access with ephemeral credentials, tenant isolation, and proactive breach testing in a real-world multi-account data pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Roles Anywhere + OIDC for short-lived, tenant-scoped credentials
- Lake Formation per-tenant access controls
- Cross-account trust with least privilege
- CMK rotation and key policy governance
- Automated breach simulations, revocation, comprehensive auditing

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
